; energy_partial_overflow: a partial sum leaves the i64 range even though
; the exact total is representable.
;
; linear = {0: i64::MAX, 1: 5, 2: -10}, sample = [1, 1, 1].
; Sorted key order: h = i64::MAX, then i64::MAX + 5 overflows before the
; -10 term could bring the total back to i64::MAX - 5. Every partial sum
; is checked (HLF.md "Accumulation order"), so ENERGY must raise rather
; than return the exact total.

PUSH 3
BQMX r0
PUSH 0
PUSH 9223372036854775807
SETLINE r0
PUSH 1
PUSH 5
SETLINE r0
PUSH 2
PUSH -10
SETLINE r0

PUSH 3
BSMX r1
PUSH 0
PUSH 1
SETLINE r1
PUSH 1
PUSH 1
SETLINE r1
PUSH 2
PUSH 1
SETLINE r1

ENERGY r0 r1
HALT
